  "summary_en": "Canada's 2026 national AI strategy, \"AI for All\", sets six pillars: protection and trust, skills, adoption, sovereign infrastructure, national champions and international alliances. It is mainly general AI and industrial policy. Robotics appears only as a priority sector (manufacturing and robotics, autonomous transport, precision agriculture) with no robot-specific governance rules.",
